 behavior in squaring operations (see comment at line 270-272: \"An important case to remember: square will have Arc::as_ptr(&x) == Arc::as_ptr(&y). The `expr_to_idx` will ensure only one recursive call is done to prevent exponential behavior.\")\n\n**`add_expr` Method (Lines 169-298):**\n\n```rust\npub fn add_expr(&mut self, expr: &SymbolicExpression<F>) -> usize {\n    // Fast path: check if we've seen this exact Arc pointer before\n    let ptr = expr as *const SymbolicExpression<F>;\n    if let Some(&idx) = self.expr_to_idx.get(&ptr) {  // Line 172-173\n        return idx;\n    }\n\n    let idx = match expr {\n        SymbolicExpression::Variable(var) => \n            self.intern_node(SymbolicExpressionNode::Variable(*var)),\n        // ... handle other cases with structural deduplication and algebraic simplifications\n    };\n\n    self.expr_to_idx.insert(ptr, idx);  // Line 296\n    idx\n}\n\nfn intern_node(&mut self, node: SymbolicExpressionNode<F>) -> usize {\n    *self.node_to_idx.entry(node.clone()).or_insert_with(|| {\n        let idx = self.nodes.len();\n        self.nodes.push(node);\n        idx\n    })\n}\n```\n\n**How It Works:**\n\n1. **Two-level deduplication** (lines 144-147):\n   - **Level 1 (fast path):** Arc pointer caching via `expr_to_idx` - same Arc = guaranteed same index\n   - **Level 2 (structural):** `node_to_idx` - catches semantically identical nodes with different Arc pointers\n\n2. **Algebraic Simplifications Performed** (lines 136-142 documentation):\n   - Constant folding: `a + b → c`, `a - b → c`, `a * b → c`, `-a → c` (for constants)\n   - Neutral elements: `x + 0 → x`, `0 + x → x`, `x - 0 → x`, `x * 1 → x`, `1 * x → x`\n   - Absorbing elements: `x * 0 → 0`, `0 * x → 0`\n   - Normalization: `x + (-y) → x - y`, `x - (-y) → x + y`\n\n3. **Recursively processes children** (lines 193-194, 226-227, 253, 273-274) while maintaining both caches\n\n4. **Round 0 Usage** (from `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerochec