de—specifically whether the Round 0 logup kernel needs modifications. The kernel currently takes the rules as a parameter, so with pre-computed rules we'd just pass them from the proving key instead of compiling them fresh each time.\n\nLet me map out the exact locations in the pre-batch code I need to work with, since I'll be reverting to that state first. I'm looking at where the constraint evaluation happens in Phase 1 and Phase 2, and how the current batch implementation structures the AirDataGpu struct. Building the parallelization strategy...\n\nThe issue is that `batch_sp_poly` needs concurrent writes from multiple threads, so I need to either partition the vector upfront with `split_at_mut`, use interior mutability with a mutex (though that's expensive), or pre-allocate and handle indexing carefully—I'm leaning toward splitting the work by trace index to avoid contention.\n\nActually, the cleanest solution is to have each parallel task return its computed polynomials as a tuple with the trace index, then collect all results and assign them afterward in a single-threaded pass.\n\nNow I'm assigning the computed polynomials back into the batch array based on their trace indices and types. Once that's done, I can move forward with writing out the implementation plan.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1801,"cache_read_input_tokens":87956,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1801},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b7092ff3-dad3-4115-bd08-06aa847648b3","uuid":"f102ca0f-7b7e-4c13-ac8d-0bc60e975c8b"}
